---
title: Fish and Chips
description: British classic
course: Main
servings: 2
locale: en_GB
prep time: 20m
cook time: 25m
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: British
tags:
- seafood
- savoury
- main-course
- british
---

Soak the @maris piper or desiree potatoes{750%g}(peeled and sliced into thick chips) chips in a bowl of water for at least ~{30%minutes} (or overnight) to remove excess starch.

Mix the dry ingredients (@plain flour{50%g}, @cornflour{50%g}, @baking powder{1%tsp}, and @?turmeric{1%tsp}) in a bowl. Remove and set aside 1 tbsp on a plate. Gradually add the @beer or sparkling water{150%ml} to the bowl and whisk to form a smooth batter. Add extra flour if too thin.

Preheat a #deep fat fryer{} to 150°C.

Drain the chips and dry thoroughly on kitchen towels. Fry the chips for 8 to ~{10%minutes} until crisp, but do not allow them to brown.

Increase oil temperature to 190°C.

Pat the @haddock (or other white fish) boneless filets{2} dry with kitchen towels, toss in the reserved turmeric flour mix, and dip in the batter.

Fry the fish (without the deep fat fryer basket) for 6 to ~{8%minutes} (depending on thickness) until golden and crisp.

Fry the chips for ~{5%minutes} until crisp and golden.